origin: extracted from milkv-duo/duo-buildroot-sdk-v2, cleaned for Linux 7.0
license: see LICENSE in this dir (driver); firmware NOT included (license unknown)
kernel: version-gated at 7.0/6.19 by upstream; verify on newer stable at build time
build: BUILD_DIR subdir via build.sh out-of-tree hook (CONFIG_PLATFORM_CVITEK=y preset)
verified: builds clean on 7.2.10 (riscv64 gcc 10.3) -> aic8800_fdrv.ko,
  aic8800_bsp.ko, aic8800_btlpm.ko
RUNTIME HAZARD (found 2026-10-11, QEMU): aic8800_bsp.ko loads fine, but
  aic8800_fdrv.ko PANICS the kernel during insmod when the WiFi chip and its
  DT node are absent: "Oops - load access fault [#1]" inside module_init
  (rwnx_mod_init -> aicbsp_set_subsys / aicsmac_driver_register, which
  dereference a bad pointer when no hardware is present). Likely
  QEMU-specific (no chip, no DT node) - UNVERIFIED on real HW.
  => Never auto-load fdrv. Only packages/userspace-src/.../milkv-load-wifi
     loads it, with a loud warning, by hand, on the board only.
7.2 port fixes (ours, minimal, in-tree):
  - dropped stale #include <linux/of_gpio.h> x3 (header removed 6.x; only
    legacy gpio_* used, still present)
  - rwnx_msg_tx.c: +#include <linux/string.h>; strncpy -> strscpy
  - rwnx_platform.c: strncpy -> strscpy (return unused, NUL kept)
  - cfg80211 net_device -> wireless_dev migration: 9 op callbacks take
    wdev + shim to netdev; call sites pass &vif->wdev / ieee80211_ptr
  - rwnx_tdls.c: flattened mgmt->u.action.u.X -> mgmt->u.action.X;
    tdls_discover_resp.action_code -> u.action.action_code (per in-tree mac80211)
